  "title": "The $50B Dealer Tax: What Your Stack Really Costs",
  "summary": "Every titled-vehicle dealership in the country runs a pile of sixteen vendor categories that costs $170,000 to $300,000 a year per rooftop and still fails to answer the buyer or close the deal as a system. Two of those layers, the lead funnel and the back office, are collapsible this quarter with software that already ships. Running both recovers $70,000 to $200,000 a year per store.",
